<p class="lesson-lead">
    Last lesson you pressed Play, walked into range, and the turret did not fire a shot — it
    fired a <em>stream</em>. Nothing you wrote is broken. Your range check is a
    <em>condition</em>, and it runs every frame, so every frame it called your firing method and
    the turret fired at your frame rate. Today you give it a memory: a field holding the moment
    it last fired, and a condition that refuses to fire again until enough time has passed. The
    fix has more than one honest answer, and you are going to pick one and defend it.
</p>

